<title>USA: Farm Credit Banks Funding to offer $1.87 bln bonds.</title>
<headline>Farm Credit Banks Funding to offer $1.87 bln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Farm Credit Banks Funding Corp on Friday announced it will offer two issues of Federal Farm Credit Banks Consolidated Systemwide Bonds totaling $1.872 billion.</p>
<p>The issues will be dated and delivered on October 1, 1996.</p>
<p>Bonds maturing on October 1, 1996, total $2.351 billion. The proceeds of the new financings will be used to retire the maturing bonds and finance operations.</p>
<p>--U.S. corporate bond unit, 212-859-1672</p>
</text>
